    {
      "id": "c6f97ae8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 56,
      "y": 3614,
      "width": 1448,
      "height": 44,
      "text": "SDK implementation gap (not a spec gap): modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk \u2014 mcp/shared/session.py\n_receive_loop dispatches server\u2192client requests with `await _received_request(responder)` inline \u2014 blocking the loop for the handler's full duration.\nThe MCP spec doesn't mandate this; it's an implementation choice. Fix: `task_group.start_soon(_received_request, responder)` \u2014 one line.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#3d1a80",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "fontStyle": "normal"
    }
  ],
